<mxCell id="note_0" value="Browser = SocialChannelsPage + socialService + Axios (/collaborator/profile?tab=social; also WalletPage). Initial GET is omitted. JWT runs before controller; DTO checks platform, integer followers &gt;= 0 and boolean primary. No RolesGuard or KYC gate is bound here." style="text;html=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=19;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacing=0;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="45" y="2595" width="2750" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note_1" value="Expanded path adds a new primary channel. If isPrimary is false, skip clearing old flags. Multiple channels on one platform are allowed; no count cap or unique URL/platform constraint is defined. Followers are entered manually; no OAuth/platform follower lookup or channel-ownership verification runs." style="text;html=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=19;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacing=0;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="45" y="2645" width="2750" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note_2" value="Profile total is recalculated using SUM over all owned rows after add/delete; absent profile is not created (updateMany count 0). Channel, primary reset and aggregate/profile writes are separate, not a transaction. A later failure can leave earlier writes committed; concurrent calls do not guarantee one primary." style="text;html=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=19;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacing=0;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="45" y="2700" width="2750" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note_3" value="DELETE /social-channels/:id and PATCH /:id/primary read the channel, return 404 if absent or 403 for another owner. Delete is permanent, recalculates totals and does not choose a replacement primary. setPrimary clears old flags then marks the selected row; general URL/follower editing has no endpoint here." style="text;html=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=19;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacing=0;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="45" y="2755" width="2750" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note_4" value="UI offers TikTok, Facebook, YouTube, Instagram, Threads and Zalo; the API enum also accepts Telegram, Shopee Video, Lemon8 and Other. First-row display fallback is not a stored primary flag. Channel rows reference User; no Profile-to-channel foreign key exists. Duplicate rows can double-count followers." style="text;html=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=19;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacing=0;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="45" y="2810" width="2750" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel>